From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:42:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Explain what went wrong when the game crashed

The Logs tab now says what a crash was, without a connection. After a
run ends, the launcher reads the game's crash report, the JVM's own
hs_err file and the end of the log, and matches them against rules for
the usual causes: out of memory, the wrong Java version, missing or
duplicate mods, mods for another game version, failed mixins, a
software renderer and more. Each finding gets a plain explanation, the
line it was found on, and where it helps a button to the Java settings
or the instance folder. Picking an older log from the list runs the same
rules against it. Files from an earlier run than the log are ignored,
so an old crash report is not blamed for a new crash.

The rules report an id and what they captured; the words are in the
frontend, so they can be translated. mclo.gs analysis in the console is
unchanged.

Adapted from Noctrinth (https://github.com/Everelsu/Noctrinth).
